9119e6a9-c1b3-4224-aa41-e0f91ae1afe3.extCompDefTitle:
&lt;title&gt;
                The TSF shall derive shared cryptographic keys with input from multiple parties in accordance with specified cryptographic key agreement algorithms
                &lt;assignable&gt;cryptographic algorithm&lt;/assignable&gt;
                and specified cryptographic parameters
                &lt;assignable&gt;cryptographic parameters&lt;/assignable&gt;
                that meet the following:
                &lt;assignable&gt;list of standards&lt;/assignable&gt;.
              &lt;/title&gt;

0f3aad79-2d86-4ca8-95fa-180994e42a16.extCompDefTitle:
&lt;title&gt;
                The TSF shall implement the IPsec protocol ESP as defined by RFC 4303 using the cryptographic 
			algorithms
                &lt;assignable&gt;cryptographic algorithms&lt;/assignable&gt;
                together with a Secure Hash Algorithm (SHA)-based HMAC.
              &lt;/title&gt;

03d1f607-41c3-420b-bbea-a7833350e49a.extCompDefTitle:
&lt;title&gt;
                The TSF shall implement the protocol:
                &lt;assignable&gt;key exchange protocol&lt;/assignable&gt;.
              &lt;/title&gt;

7505c5ba-2b2d-40fa-8a07-5a2a26497fc7.extCompDefTitle:
&lt;title&gt;
                The TSF shall ensure the encrypted payload in the
                &lt;assignable&gt;key exchange protocol&lt;/assignable&gt;
                protocol uses the cryptographic algorithms
                &lt;assignable&gt;cryptographic algorithms&lt;/assignable&gt;
                and no other algorithm.
              &lt;/title&gt;

0d16f71a-7271-4397-a652-6a3c98d8d770.extCompDefTitle:
&lt;title&gt;
                The TSF shall ensure that
                &lt;assignable&gt;key exchange protocol lifetime configuration rules&lt;/assignable&gt;.
              &lt;/title&gt;

48e4ed1f-32bc-4c5d-a34f-6c49661b3239.extCompDefTitle:
&lt;title&gt;
                The TSF shall ensure that all IKE protocols implement DH groups
                &lt;assignable&gt;DH Groups&lt;/assignable&gt;.
              &lt;/title&gt;

5a6a1474-5de8-4c8a-bc4b-348ab628eaef.extCompDefTitle:
&lt;title&gt;
                The TSF shall ensure that all IKE protocols perform peer authentication using a
                &lt;assignable&gt;IKE peer authentication algorithm&lt;/assignable&gt;
                that use X.509v3 certificates that conform to RFC 4945 and
                &lt;assignable&gt;other IKE peer authentication mechanism&lt;/assignable&gt;.
              &lt;/title&gt;

19d27f9a-1e07-4388-8115-7e85449adddb.extCompDefTitle:
&lt;title&gt;
                The TSF shall not establish an SA if the
                &lt;assignable&gt;specific certificate reference identifier&lt;/assignable&gt;
                and
                &lt;assignable&gt;other certificate reference identifier type&lt;/assignable&gt;
                contained in a certificate does
			not match the expected value(s) for the entity attempting to establish a connection.
              &lt;/title&gt;

b7e3e881-f376-4abf-ab04-b7cdb8a0f5c1.extCompDefTitle:
&lt;title&gt;
                The TSF shall provide
                &lt;assignable&gt;protected storage type&lt;/assignable&gt;
                protected storage for asymmetric private keys and
                &lt;assignable&gt;secrets to be stored&lt;/assignable&gt;.
              &lt;/title&gt;

a2b8c7b6-e5f2-4272-8549-5388e7476c39.extCompDefTitle:
&lt;title&gt;
                The TSF shall support the capability of
                &lt;assignable&gt;capability for acquiring keys&lt;/assignable&gt;
                upon request of
                &lt;assignable&gt;entity requesting storage&lt;/assignable&gt;.
              &lt;/title&gt;

5df0315c-434c-46d9-9360-fb91ba3158f6.extCompDefTitle:
&lt;title&gt;
                The TSF shall be capable of destroying keys/secrets in the protected storage
					upon request of
                &lt;assignable&gt;authorized subject&lt;/assignable&gt;.
              &lt;/title&gt;

1f9b1df0-6d0d-45f8-835d-d79d0a87b607.extCompDefTitle:
&lt;title&gt;
                The TSF shall encrypt
                &lt;assignable&gt;types of key material&lt;/assignable&gt;
                using
                &lt;assignable&gt;cryptographic algorithm&lt;/assignable&gt;.
              &lt;/title&gt;

7f433fb9-5d01-4ef9-8c91-06cf38ac7a9b.extCompDefTitle:
&lt;title&gt;
                The TSF shall protect the integrity of any encrypted
                &lt;assignable&gt;types of key material&lt;/assignable&gt;
                by using
                &lt;assignable&gt;integrity protection mechanism&lt;/assignable&gt;.
              &lt;/title&gt;

db5e1e9d-eb64-4c50-bcb1-06a5df2a5893.extCompDefTitle:
&lt;title&gt;
                The TSF shall support importing keys/key material using
                &lt;assignable&gt;import mechanism&lt;/assignable&gt;.
              &lt;/title&gt;

a3406b4a-5810-42a3-b318-55316886b549.extCompDefTitle:
&lt;title&gt;
                The TSF shall verify the integrity of imported keys/key material using
                &lt;assignable&gt;integrity verification method&lt;/assignable&gt;.
              &lt;/title&gt;

a2d5b8d9-e797-4147-80a5-f51a8d6df20c.extCompDefTitle:
&lt;title&gt;
                The TSF shall implement a trusted execution environment that conforms to the following
					standard:
                &lt;assignable&gt;Trusted Execution Environment standard&lt;/assignable&gt;
                and make this TEE available to tenant software.
              &lt;/title&gt;

d34a895d-b606-4aac-95eb-524495ca2913.extCompDefTitle:
&lt;title&gt;
                The TSF shall consider password and
                &lt;assignable&gt;other authentication mechanisms&lt;/assignable&gt;
                as critical authentication mechanisms.
              &lt;/title&gt;

7fc9496c-f71a-42f7-91e9-5cf3ee537b4d.extCompDefTitle:
&lt;title&gt;
                The TSF shall support the following for the Password Authentication Factor:
                &lt;ol type="1"&gt;&lt;li&gt;
                    Passwords shall be able to be composed of any combination of
                    &lt;assignable&gt;characters sets&lt;/assignable&gt;,
						numbers, and special characters:
                    &lt;assignable&gt;special characters&lt;/assignable&gt;.
                  &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;
                    Password length of at least
                    &lt;assignable&gt;an integer greater than or equal to 14&lt;/assignable&gt;
                    characters shall be 
						supported.
                  &lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;&lt;/title&gt;

9c57b4ad-2c09-4dda-a09b-53c0453c7e49.extCompDefTitle:
&lt;title&gt;
                The integrity of platform firmware shall be rooted in
                &lt;assignable&gt;platform firmware root of trust&lt;/assignable&gt;.
              &lt;/title&gt;

bd72f52c-e8cd-4e60-afa9-b64050542858.extCompDefTitle:
&lt;title&gt;
                The integrity of all mutable platform firmware outside of the platform integrity root specified in FPT_ROT_EXT.1 shall be verified prior to
                &lt;selectables&gt;&lt;selectable&gt;execution&lt;/selectable&gt;&lt;selectable&gt;use&lt;/selectable&gt;&lt;selectable&gt;or access to TSF data&lt;/selectable&gt;&lt;/selectables&gt;
                through:
                &lt;assignable&gt;method for extending the platform integrity root&lt;/assignable&gt;.
              &lt;/title&gt;

e2662117-76d5-456c-b425-8431b362637b.extCompDefTitle:
&lt;title&gt;
                The TOE shall take the following actions if an integrity check specified in FPT_ROT_EXT.2.1 fails:
                &lt;selectables linebreak="yes"&gt;&lt;selectable&gt;Stop all execution, or&lt;/selectable&gt;&lt;selectable&gt;
                    Notify an
                    &lt;selectables&gt;&lt;selectable id="sel-rot2-admin-notify"&gt;administrator&lt;/selectable&gt;&lt;selectable&gt;user&lt;/selectable&gt;&lt;/selectables&gt;
                    by
                    &lt;selectables&gt;&lt;selectable id="sel-rot2-audit"&gt;generating an audit event&lt;/selectable&gt;&lt;selectable&gt;&lt;assignable&gt;other notification methods&lt;/assignable&gt;&lt;/selectable&gt;&lt;/selectables&gt;, and
                    &lt;selectables linebreak="yes"&gt;&lt;selectable&gt;Stop all execution&lt;/selectable&gt;&lt;selectable&gt;Shut down, or&lt;/selectable&gt;&lt;selectable id="sel-rot2-recovery"&gt;Initiate a recovery process as specified in FPT_RVR_EXT.1&lt;/selectable&gt;&lt;selectable&gt;Skip all instructions that failed the integrity check and continue execution&lt;/selectable&gt;&lt;/selectables&gt;&lt;selectables linebreak="yes"&gt;&lt;selectable&gt;automatically&lt;/selectable&gt;&lt;selectable id="sel-rot2-admin-config"&gt;in accordance with administrator-configurable policy&lt;/selectable&gt;&lt;selectable&gt;
                        by express determination of an
                        &lt;selectables&gt;&lt;selectable id="sel-rot2-admin-det"&gt;administrator&lt;/selectable&gt;&lt;selectable id="sel-rot2-user-det"&gt;user&lt;/selectable&gt;&lt;/selectables&gt;&lt;/selectable&gt;&lt;/selectables&gt;&lt;/selectable&gt;&lt;/selectables&gt;.
              &lt;/title&gt;

638d145d-7272-493f-a44e-97ae94115460.extCompDefTitle:
&lt;title&gt;
                The TOE shall take the following actions if an integrity check specified in FPT_ROT_EXT.3.1 fails:
                &lt;ol type="1"&gt;&lt;li&gt;Halt,&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;
                    Notify an
                    &lt;selectables&gt;&lt;selectable&gt;administrator&lt;/selectable&gt;&lt;selectable&gt;user&lt;/selectable&gt;&lt;/selectables&gt;
                    by
                    &lt;assignable&gt;notification method&lt;/assignable&gt;, and
                  &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;selectables linebreak="yes" onlyone="yes"&gt;&lt;selectable&gt;Stop all execution and shut down&lt;/selectable&gt;&lt;selectable&gt;Continue execution without the integrity-compromised component&lt;/selectable&gt;&lt;selectable&gt;Continue execution&lt;/selectable&gt;&lt;/selectables&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;selectables linebreak="yes" onlyone="yes"&gt;&lt;selectable&gt;in accordance with administrator-configurable policy&lt;/selectable&gt;&lt;selectable&gt;
                        by express determination of an
                        &lt;selectables&gt;&lt;selectable&gt;administrator&lt;/selectable&gt;&lt;selectable&gt;user&lt;/selectable&gt;&lt;/selectables&gt;&lt;/selectable&gt;&lt;/selectables&gt;&lt;/li&gt;.
                &lt;/ol&gt;&lt;/title&gt;

0dd30e01-b0e1-4a3e-b447-d2d7ef659e84.extCompDefTitle:
&lt;title&gt;
                The TSF shall implement a mechanism for recovering from boot firmware failure consisting of
                &lt;assignable&gt;recovery mechanism&lt;/assignable&gt;.
              &lt;/title&gt;

0fc709f7-fdfd-4d72-a141-b695a3744abc.extCompDefTitle:
&lt;title&gt;
                The TSF shall authenticate the source of all platform firmware updates using a 
					digital signature algorithm specified in FCS_COP.1 and using a key store 
					that contains
                &lt;selectables&gt;&lt;selectable&gt;the public key&lt;/selectable&gt;&lt;selectable&gt;hash value of the public key&lt;/selectable&gt;&lt;/selectables&gt;.
              &lt;/title&gt;

8ae24334-74c9-40fe-9a17-a123678942f9.extCompDefTitle:
&lt;title&gt;
                The TSF shall allow installation of updates only if the digital signature has been
					successfully verified as specified in FCS_COP.1 and
                &lt;assignable&gt;additional constraints on updates&lt;/assignable&gt;.
              &lt;/title&gt;

3bbf16a5-dea6-428a-a626-4c24b81f8adb.extCompDefTitle:
&lt;title&gt;
                The TOE shall take the following actions if a platform firmware integrity, authenticity, 
					or rollback-prevention check fails, or a platform firmware update fails for any other reason:
                &lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Do not install the update,&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;selectables linebreak="yes" onlyone="yes"&gt;&lt;selectable&gt;Continue execution&lt;/selectable&gt;&lt;selectable&gt;Halt&lt;/selectable&gt;&lt;selectable&gt;Stop all execution and shut down&lt;/selectable&gt;&lt;selectable&gt;Initiate recovery as specified in FPT_RVR_EXT.1&lt;/selectable&gt;&lt;/selectables&gt;&lt;selectables linebreak="yes" onlyone="yes"&gt;&lt;selectable&gt;automatically&lt;/selectable&gt;&lt;selectable&gt;in accordance with administrator-configurable policy&lt;/selectable&gt;&lt;selectable&gt;by express determination of a user&lt;/selectable&gt;&lt;/selectables&gt;, and
                &lt;selectables linebreak="yes"&gt;&lt;selectable id="sel-tud2-audit"&gt;generate an audit event&lt;/selectable&gt;&lt;selectable&gt;no other actions&lt;/selectable&gt;&lt;/selectables&gt;.
              &lt;/title&gt;

adf0fe1b-5585-47c5-8258-702b03abe8ea.extCompDefTitle:
&lt;title&gt;
                The TSF shall allow execution or use of platform firmware updates only if new platform firmware
					is integrity- and authenticity-checked using the mechanism described in FPT_ROT_EXT.2 prior to its
					execution or use, and
                &lt;assignable&gt;additional constraints on update&lt;/assignable&gt;.
              &lt;/title&gt;

a8a55aaa-4cb2-4363-a9cf-b832add19bbd.extCompDefTitle:
&lt;title&gt;
                The TOE shall take the following actions if a platform firmware update integrity, authentication, or
					rollback-prevention check fails, or a platform firmware update fails for any other reason:
                &lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Do not install the update,&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Generate an audit event (optional),&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;
                and
                &lt;selectables linebreak="yes" onlyone="yes"&gt;&lt;selectable&gt;Continue execution&lt;/selectable&gt;&lt;selectable&gt;Halt&lt;/selectable&gt;&lt;selectable&gt;Stop all execution and shut down&lt;/selectable&gt;&lt;selectable id="sel-tud3-recovery"&gt;Initiate recovery as specified in FPT_RVR_EXT.1&lt;/selectable&gt;&lt;/selectables&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;selectables linebreak="yes" onlyone="yes"&gt;&lt;selectable&gt;automatically&lt;/selectable&gt;&lt;selectable id="sel-tud3-admin-config"&gt;in accordance with administrator-configurable policy&lt;/selectable&gt;&lt;selectable&gt;by express determination of a user&lt;/selectable&gt;&lt;/selectables&gt;.
              &lt;/title&gt;

6fcdd9a0-b0fc-4095-ab03-77673828cd5c.extCompDefTitle:
&lt;title&gt;
                A user shall assert physical presence to the TSF through:
                &lt;assignable&gt;method for asserting physical presence&lt;/assignable&gt;.
              &lt;/title&gt;

0f92fb7d-151e-4a32-bdfd-15599077672b.extCompDefTitle:
&lt;title&gt;
                The TSF shall use
                &lt;assignable&gt;trusted channel protocols&lt;/assignable&gt;
                protocols with
                &lt;assignable&gt;authentication mechanism&lt;/assignable&gt;
                to provide a communication channel between itself and
                &lt;assignable&gt;external IT entities&lt;/assignable&gt;
                that is logically distinct from other communication channels, provides assured 
					identification of its end points, protects channel data from disclosure, and detects modification
					of the channel data.
              &lt;/title&gt;

b92bf1ab-2052-4f0b-8f5d-dec00811024b.extCompDefTitle:
&lt;title&gt;
                The TSF shall encrypt data for transfer between the TOE and
                &lt;assignable&gt;list of entities external to the TOE&lt;/assignable&gt;
                using a cryptographic algorithm and key size as specified in
					FCS_COP.1, and using
                &lt;assignable&gt;key establishment mechanism&lt;/assignable&gt;.
              &lt;/title&gt;
